<main class="wrap">
  <div class="lede">
    <h1>Building Jiva in the open</h1>
    <p>Jiva is a fully-local second brain for the Mac, built by one product manager who can't write the code — every line written with an AI. This is the running log of that attempt: the origin, the hard on-device audio problems, the things that broke, and the honest question of how far this goes.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="list">
    <a class="post" href="/blog/the-granola-and-claude-moment">
      <div class="date">14 September 2026 · 7 min read</div>
      <h2>The Granola-and-Claude moment that started Jiva</h2>
      <div class="sum">I used a meeting recorder and an AI side by side for months before I noticed what they could do together. Then I hit the same wall three times, and the wall turned out to be the product.</div>
    </a>
  </div>

  <p class="more">More on the way — the first thing that broke, why attribution is really an audio problem, and the honest market read.</p>
</main>

